dle the  pressure so 16 you're on the cover of  Sports Illustrated and you're the LeBron  James of baseball and now does he want  that title of the highest-paid player in  baseball does he want the added pressure  that goes along with it how does he  handle it yeah I think he does I'll  never forget writing that story now when  I reported this story of when he was 16  I didn't know it was going to be the  cover but then when I found out that it  was at first I was like what is a pretty  big ask to put a high school kid on the  cover of Si well I came away thinking  man this is a one kid he was a kid at  the time who can handle that  I think he's grown up with the spotlight  on him I think he enjoys it I don't  think there's any extra added pressure  if he's got a huge contract I think he  needs to learn how to win that's the  biggest thing I think he needs to be in  a culture where winning is the top  priority I think it would help if there  was another star player on the  team or he just didn't have to be the  guy that to leave a team entirely in  terms of being you know it's a clubhouse  leader I think getting in the right  atmosphere is gonna help him win but in  terms of pressure my goodness yeah got  to live up to a contract I don't see  that being an issue with this guy I know  we've seen man the past with a lot of  guys I think he's cut from a different  cloth  how much did how different is he then  Mike Trout when it comes to that no were  easy no I think he is different I think  you know I think Mike's a little bit  different in terms of just the attention  that he seeks or is comfortable with  I think price like I said you know  remember Dan when he was 12 or 13 these  travel teams were flying him into  tournaments to be let's face it kind of  a ringer you add somebody to your travel  team roster for some big tournament he's  been a hired gun he's been the guy that  everybody's had their eyes on Mike  didn't grow up that way  so I think it's a different atmosphere I  always say that that brace is kind of  the epitome of what is now the travel  player generation where you play more  for yourself and your skills and to be  seen then you do for winning games you  know when we grew up it was about  playing for your high school team or  your Legion team or your local little  league team those barriers are all gone  now now it's you just hired guns that's  about showcase atmospheres where it's  about your own individual ability I'm  not saying it's a bad thing when Brice  is the epitome that new generation I  play nice today at Citi Field there ton  thank you Tom Tom Verducci Sports  Illustrated senior writer also works for  a Fox and Major League Baseball network  for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience Channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show at  [Music]

